{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or trending downward, as models tend to overestimate prices in such regimes.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% when recent true outcomes show a sharp downward spike (e.g., >10% drop from prior day), to account for overshoot bias.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if forecast is >15% above recent 5-day average, reduce by 10-15% to align with historical volatility patterns.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment when sentiment > 0.5: model should respond more aggressively to positive sentiment, but cap upward adjustments at +10% to avoid overcorrection.",
    "For horizon > 15 days, apply lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, reduce forecast by 5-8% for each additional day beyond 15 to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00) and history shows low volatility, apply a smoothing filter to reduce forecast volatility by 20% to avoid overfitting to noise."
  ]
}
